.TH MURAL 7 "August 22, 2026" "mural 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
mural \- GPU wallpaper daemon and control tools
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mural
is a small Wayland wallpaper system made of a long-running renderer daemon,
.BR murald (1),
and a script-friendly control client,
.BR muralctl (1).
It requires a Wayland compositor with wlr-layer-shell support and is primarily
tested on Sway.
.PP
The daemon creates one background layer-shell surface per output, renders JPG,
PNG, and WebP wallpapers through EGL/GLES, and keeps native wallpaper library
state: shuffle bag, history, favorites, quarantine, and per-layout current
wallpapers. Favorites do not immediately change the current display; they add
extra copies of favorite paths to rebuilt shuffle bags so future random
selections choose them more often. Wallpaper navigation commands are intended
to preserve per-monitor layout semantics, so shifting wallpapers follows the
actual output layout order.
.PP
Configuration lives in
.BR mural-config (5).
The packaged user service is a systemd
.B Type=notify
unit. It enables systemd watchdog recovery by default; use a local
user-service drop-in with
.B WatchdogSec=0
when diagnosing freezes and wanting the daemon to remain stuck for inspection.
.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.TP
.B muralctl next
Show the next wallpaper set.
.TP
.B muralctl back
Show the previous wallpaper set.
.TP
.B muralctl shift forward
Move current wallpapers forward through output layout order.
.TP
.B muralctl shift back
Move current wallpapers backward through output layout order.
.TP
.B muralctl current
Show current wallpaper index, output, favorite marker, and path rows.
.TP
.B muralctl favorites
List favorite wallpaper paths.
.TP
.B muralctl query --json
Show daemon output state as JSON.
.TP
.B muralctl capabilities
Show the transition implementations and parameters compiled into the running
daemon.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mural/config
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mural
Default state directory when XDG_STATE_HOME is unset.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/systemd/user/murald.service
User-local service file when XDG_DATA_HOME is set.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/systemd/user/murald.service
Fallback user-local service file installed by the Makefile.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/murald.service.d/*.conf
User service drop-ins.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR murald (1),
.BR muralctl (1),
.BR mural-config (5),
.BR systemd.service (5)
